.TH "RTCPEERCONNECTIONICEERROREVENT.PORT" "3JS" "May 12, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent.port \- RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent:
port property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]port\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]RTCPeerConnectionIceErrorEvent\f[R] interface represents the port
number over which communication with the STUN or TURN server is taking
place.
.PP
This is \f[CR]null\f[R] if the connection hasn\(cqt been established
(\f[CR]address\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R]).
.SH VALUE
A positive integer.
.PP
\f[CR]null\f[R] if the connection hasn\(cqt been established (that is,
if \f[CR]address\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example creates a handler for \f[CR]icecandidateerror\f[R] events,
which creates human\-readable messages describing the local network
interface for the connection and the ICE server used to attempt the
connection.
It then calls a function to display those messages and the value of the
event\(cqs \f[CR]errorText\f[R] property.
.IP
.EX
pc.addEventListener(\(dqicecandidateerror\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] networkInfo = \(ga[Local interface: ${event.address}:${event.port}]\(ga;
  \f[B]const\f[R] iceServerInfo = \(ga[ICE server: ${event.url}]\(ga;

  showMessage(event.errorText, iceServerInfo, networkInfo);
});
.EE
